WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.410
- Welcome to America,

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.020
the freest country in the entire world,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.960
which we know is true because
it's a thing that people say

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.790
and you might actually believe that

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.710
until you try to build housing somewhere

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.750
or drink alcohol in public.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.583
But unfortunately,

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:16.890
America is not the freest
country in the world.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.060
In fact, according to some,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.940
it's barely in the top
20 freest countries.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.550
But the world is a diverse
place and one country's freedom

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.620
is another country's criminal violation.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.750
And there are wide swaths of activities

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.220
that are perfectly normal
in other countries,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.400
but also very, very illegal in America.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.233
So today,

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.380
let's look at some international liberties

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.820
that could get you fine or locked up

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.020
if you tried them stateside.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.420
And some of these foreign
freedoms may surprise you.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.060
But let's start with a truly
evil and dastardly product,

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.060
one that actually
specifically targets children.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.400
I'm of course talking about Kinder Eggs.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.890
Now, we like to say that
children are the future,

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:50.760
and here in America,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:51.900
the moment we find out that something

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.550
puts children in danger,

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.620
legislators pull out
all the stops to ensure

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.600
that we try to keep our kids safe.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.250
And that's why America has stood firm

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.410
to cracking down on a
grave and terrible threat

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.300
to children's health and safety posed

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.940
by toy filled chocolate eggs.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.050
Kinder Surprise Eggs,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.434
which famously contain a yellow capsule,

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.820
which contains a small toy,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.580
have been a beloved staple
for children around the world

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.160
ever since the product's
introduction in 1974

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.380
by Ferrero, the Italian company.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.610
But in the United States,

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:23.880
these toy filled treats have
been classified as dangerous

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.410
illegal contraband.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.243
And some background.

00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:27.076
In 1938,

00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:29.340
the US passed the Food,
Drug, and Cosmetic Act,

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.920
which empowered government
agencies to regulate food safety,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.050
and under consumer
safety regulations issued

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.690
by the FDA and the Consumer
Product Safety Commission,

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.370
the sale and distribution of any food

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:42.060
with a quote "non-nutritive
object embedded" is prohibited,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.090
and that includes toys found
inside confectionary items.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.310
Now, although you can
find Kinder Surprise Eggs

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.780
in Canada and Mexico,

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.310
don't try to bring them into this country

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.320
or you risk serious fines.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.770
In 2011, the US Customs and
Border Protection, the CBP,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.710
seized more than 60,000
Kinder Eggs from travelers'

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.960
baggage and international mail shipments,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.600
more than twice that number from 2010.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.990
This caused the CBP to issue
a press release in 2012

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.030
warning people to try to stop sneaking

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.560
chocolate eggs into the country.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.600
Quote, "Also known as Kinder Eggs,

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.760
these chocolate treats
may be cute and seasonal,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.530
but they are too dangerous to children

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.540
to be imported legally into the US,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.160
The problem is the small plastic toy

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.390
inside the Kinder Egg.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.560
While sold in many countries,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.120
this product is banned from the US

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.460
because young children can choke on it."

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.480
Now, some people have argued

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.950
that these Kinder Eggs are not a risk

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.310
to European children and Canadian
children because European

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.465
and Canadian children are
smarter than US children.

00:02:35.465 --> 00:02:36.600
(man giggling)

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.900
Now, a few months after the
CBP released that statement,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.370
a married couple from Seattle was

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.490
detained at the Canadian
border when the pair was caught

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.650
with six Kinder Eggs from Vancouver.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.750
The couple was unaware that
they were in possession

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.110
of illegal ovarian contraband
and was even more shocked

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.620
that each egg carried a
penalty of $2,500 per egg.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.700
Now, luckily for that couple,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.900
they were let off with a warning,

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.510
but not to worry American
Kinder fans because in 2018,

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.300
Ferrero introduced a
modified Kinder Joy Egg

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.070
that complies with US regulations.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:05.903
Crucially,

00:03:05.903 --> 00:03:08.460
the Kinder Joy is not actually
an egg-shaped chocolate.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.100
It's half a chocolate egg
with wafer bits inside

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.320
while the toy is kept on
the other side of the egg,

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.700
away from the edible bit,

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.940
which I guess is suitable for
hapless American children.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.010
And despite the fear
surrounding Kinder Eggs,

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.210
there's little evidence that these

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.730
chocolate delights are
as dangerous as claimed.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.130
Now, there have been seven
reported child deaths

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.350
between 1989 and 2016,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.300
a relatively tiny number in the face

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.890
of billions of eggs sold.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.170
And furthermore, the
packaging warns parents

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.270
that the eggs are not suitable
for kids under the age

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.280
of three and supervision is recommended.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.190
But let's not leave
food-based illegality because

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.990
while Americans remain deeply divided

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.630
on a wide variety of issues,

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.490
there's one thing that
most of us can agree on

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.310
and that's that life begins at cheese.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:52.560
Now, over the last 40
years, our love of cheese,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.020
much like our waistbands, has grown.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.390
Between 1977 and 2020,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.820
we Americans have increased
our annual cheese consumption

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.390
from 16 pounds to 40 pounds every year.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.210
And I'm probably responsible
for about half of that.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.820
So needless to say, we
Americans love our cheese,

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.320
whether it's on pizza, burgers,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.050
or in the form of 64 Jesus-infused

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.850
slices of American cheese.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.880
- Have you been up all
night eating cheese?

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.770
- I think I'm blind.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.230
- But if you are taking a
cheese tour of the world,

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.030
be careful what you bring
back to the United States

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.770
because your love of cheese might just

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.150
put you in legal jeopardy.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.470
- You guys enjoying that cheese?

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.700
It's unpasteurized.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.500
It's illegal in this country.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.600
- In fact, many raw,
soft cheeses from France

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.490
like bleu de gex, roquefort,

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.820
or reblochon are illegal
in the United States

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.610
due to the FDA's strict
cheese production regulations.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.443
Under these rules,

00:04:42.443 --> 00:04:45.120
cheeses made with raw unpasteurized milk

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.670
is illegal to import or
sell in the United States

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.490
unless it has been aged
for at least 60 days.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.050
The reasoning is, of course, food safety,

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.940
namely to minimize the risk of foodborne

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.000
contagions like listeria,
salmonella, and E. coli.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.290
And after 60 days,

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.510
the acids and salts in raw milk cheese

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.790
coupled with the aging
process begin to naturally

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.070
kill these types of harmful bacteria.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.630
But here's the thing,

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.310
anyone who has ever been to France

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.910
knows that the cheese is
so, so much better there.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.530
And it's not just raw cheese.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.080
The FDA has also cracked
down on certain cheeses just

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.220
because they contain
too many live insects.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.750
That's the case with casu martzu,

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.360
a traditional Sardinian sheeps milk cheese

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.853
that's intentionally
infested with live maggots.

00:05:26.853 --> 00:05:30.030
Casu martzu, which literally
means rotten cheese,

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.430
gets its special flavor
from being left to rot out

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.710
among swarms of fly larvae.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.930
And while I'm told this
hellish looking cheese

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.460
is actually quite delicious,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:39.690
it turns out that eating maggots

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.820
is actually a tremendous health risk,

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.230
earning the cheese the nickname

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.910
the world's most dangerous cheese.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.460
And as a result, casu martzu
is not only illegal in the US,

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.680
but in the entire European Union.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.940
But here's the thing,

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.120
anyone who has ever been to
Sardinia knows the maggot

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.390
filled cheese is just
so much better there,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.640
but the friendship also have
been on the receiving end

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.890
of big government's
anti bug eating crusade.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.620
In 2013, the FDA angered
American cheesephiles

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.500
by blocking the import of
French mimolette cheese

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.370
just because the cheese is

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.200
naturally infested with cheese mites.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.720
And while most cheese makers
consider the mites a nuisance,

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.370
mimolette producers actually encourage

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.140
the microscopic critters to burrow

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.450
into the rind in order
to help the cheese ripen

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.502
and produce its distinctively
sweet, earthy flavor.

00:06:21.502 --> 00:06:22.950
(man humming)

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.240
Mitey.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.250
But the FDA has determined that eating too

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.350
many mites could cause
an allergic reaction,

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.140
resulting in the ban of
the gouda-like cheese.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.870
And though the FDA has no
legal limit on cheese mites,

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.880
the agency indicated
target of no more than

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.320
six mites per square inch,

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.840
which mimolette simply cannot meet.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.870
So, what are the consequences
of contraband cheese?

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.250
- We got a tip about some food

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.500
entering the country illegally.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.000
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.950
- Well, the failure to
declare food products

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:53.460
on your customs forms can
result in fines of up to $10,000

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.480
and your unlawful cheese will
be seized, but be forewarned.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.920
There is a thriving black market

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.210
for cheese in the United States

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.880
and illegal cheese is very
much on the government's radar.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.680
The Department of Homeland
Security, you know,

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.360
the post 9/11 agency responsible

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.940
for protecting the country
from terrorism and Kinder Eggs,

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.850
has helped to bust cheese
smuggling rings into Canada,

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.090
but unless you're a large
scale cheese smuggler,

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.220
you're probably not
looking at any jail time.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.240
- Wow.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.073
You got me.

00:07:19.073 --> 00:07:20.880
Good one, making me
think I was gonna, like,

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.260
die in federal prison.

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:23.760
Ah, that's super funny.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.320
You scamps.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.220
- So worst case scenario,

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.570
you're probably looking at a fine

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.480
and suffering the on
way of eating your dry,

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.430
cheeseless crackers alone.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.050
But let's leave the food world and get

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.870
into something that probably
makes a little bit more sense.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:40.110
Now, a source of pride for
the baby boomer generation is

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.950
that everything was dangerous
and no one seemed to care.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.080
Yes, that golden era
where we lined our walls

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.790
with cancerous asbestos,

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:50.220
medical professionals smoked in hospitals,

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.540
and people sold chemistry sets

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.610
to children that contained real uranium.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.110
So of course, as a society,

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.960
we used to let kids hurl giant darts

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:01.290
into the air with impunity and
call it a national pastime.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.030
That's the story of lawn darts,

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:05.670
which have been illegal in
the United States since 1988

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.130
after being linked to
thousands of injuries

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.620
and the deaths of at least three children.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.800
Lawn darts, known as
javelin darts or jarts,

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.130
was a popular lawn game
in the mid 20th century.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.990
The gameplay was actually
quite straightforward.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.330
Players would take turns
tossing giant darts

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:24.660
into a circle placed about 35
feet away, call it corn hole,

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:27.960
but with giant razor
sharp darts raining down

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:31.410
from the sky instead of soft bean bags.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.730
Now, unfortunately,

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:36.810
throwing a giant metal dart
is a tremendous safety hazard

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.690
and government regulators
eventually began to take notice.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.820
- This isn't child's play according

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.440
to the Food and Drug administration.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.540
- The US's first attempt
to outlaw the game

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.270
was strenuously posed
by jart manufacturers

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.820
who fought the proposed FDA ban in court.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.520
In 1970, manufacturers
actually won a compromise

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.080
that would allow the sale of lawn darts

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:58.080
so long as it was, one,
only marketed to adults,

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.630
then two, the product was no
longer sold in toy stores,

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.150
and three, the product
contained warning labels

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.180
alerting consumers to keep it
out of the reach of children.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:07.770
But unfortunately, these
compromised measures

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.210
were insufficient to prevent tragedy

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.490
for aerospace engineer David Snow.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.690
In April 1987,

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.430
Snow's seven year old daughter, Michelle,

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:16.290
was killed by a lawn dart thrown by one

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:18.180
of her nine year old brother's playmates

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.300
in the backyard of their home
in Riverside, California.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.760
The dart hit her head with
approximately 23,000 pounds

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.960
of pressure per square inch

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.390
and Snow's daughter died three days later.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:29.010
The grieving father then
made it his mission to

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.870
lobby public officials to take lawn darts

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.130
off the market for good.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.480
Snow brought his complaint to the

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:35.070
Consumer Product Safety Commission who

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.530
were persuaded to
investigate Snow's claims.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.020
The Commission discovered that
over a period of eight years,

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:44.310
lawn darts had sent 6,100
people to the emergency room,

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.880
81% of those cases involved
kids aged 15 or younger,

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.740
half were 10 or younger,

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.110
and many had suffered
permanent injury disability

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.310
or even death.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.860
In 1988, Snow prevailed in his crusade.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.540
The Commission voted
two to one to prohibit

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.810
the sale of all lawn darts and
had them removed from stores

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.180
in time for that year's Christmas.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:07.080
And Canada also outlawed
lawn darts in July of 1989.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.730
Now, if you wanna play
traditional lawn darts,

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:09.810
you'll have to hop on a plane

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.210
and visit the European Union
where the game is still legal.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.650
But here in the US,

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.500
you can find a legal version
with a modified plastic

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:19.056
blunt tip that replaces
the sharp metal tip

00:10:19.056 --> 00:10:21.810
'cause that makes quite a lot more sense.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:22.950
But that takes us to something that's

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.650
arguably even more dangerous, smoking.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:27.210
Now, for most of the 20th century,

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.770
cigarette smoking was glorified

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.200
as the ultimate embodiment
of the American West,

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.660
things like tough guys,
rebels without a cause.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.910
In advertising, doctors
endorsed their favorite brands

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.590
while we were told that women

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.270
found smoking men irresistible.

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.550
But this image of health and sex appeal

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.800
slowly began to change starting in 1964

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.650
after the US Surgeon General
stated definitively that yes,

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.450
smoking tobacco can be fatal.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.000
And research shows that flavored
cigarettes largely appeal

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.740
to and are disproportionately used

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:55.770
by those under 18 years of age.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.750
- That is not how to inhale, Bobby.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.100
You're hot boxing it!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.740
- So to help combat
youth smoking, in 2009,

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.750
the FDA banned the sale
of flavored cigarettes,

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:06.510
including cloves, cinnamon,
candy and fruit flavors

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:10.080
pursuant to the Family Smoking
Prevention and Control Act,

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.300
though menthol cigarettes
were exempted from the ban

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.400
as well as non-cigarette tobacco products

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.080
like electronic cigarettes, cigars,

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.730
smokeless, tobacco, and hookah.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:19.020
But the US is not alone here

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.400
as countries with policies banning

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.310
some or all types of flavored
cigarettes include Canada,

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.790
Brazil, Ethiopia, Uganda,
Senegal, Niger, Mauritania,

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.370
and 28 member states
of the European Union,

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.200
Moldova, Turkey, and Singapore.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.060
As for everyone else, well,

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.340
not only are flavored
cigarettes completely legal

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.840
in the vast majority of countries,

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.700
but the US ban on cloves actually

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:40.620
created an international incident.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.420
In April 2010, Indonesia,

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:44.520
the world's top producer
of clove cigarettes

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.080
and the source of the vast majority

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.940
of those smoked in the US,

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.970
filed a trade dispute with
the World Trade Organization.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:51.803
In its claim,

00:11:51.803 --> 00:11:54.090
Indonesia argued that the US
ban illegally discriminated

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.250
against foreign products
of flavored tobacco

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.020
and created an unlawful advantage

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.660
for domestic tobacco manufacturers.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.450
In September 2011, the WTO agreed,

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.550
finding that the ban was
indeed discriminatory

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.440
because it prohibited clove cigarettes

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:10.410
while allowing the sale of
American menthol cigarettes.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.020
The opinion was affirmed
on appeal in 2012.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.970
This ruling gave Indonesia
the right to retaliate

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.370
until either the US
changed its law to comply

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.200
or the two sides reached a settlement.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.220
And in 2014,

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.010
the two countries reached a
final settlement on the issue,

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.210
ending their dispute.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.200
Under the settlement,

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.690
the US agreed it would not
arbitrarily discriminate

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.640
against certain Indonesian
tobacco products

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.120
and promised to work with
Indonesia on other trade issues.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.670
Now, a decade after the
flavored tobacco ban,

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:38.610
public health advocates seemed
to have been vindicated.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.387
A 2020 study published in the

00:12:40.387 --> 00:12:41.820
"Journal of Adolescent Health"

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.950
found that the flavor ban was effective

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:46.320
at reducing cigarette
use among young people.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.520
In April of 2022,

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.260
the FDA took additional steps against

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.450
flavored tobacco products
by proposing a ban

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.070
on the sales of menthol cigarettes

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.050
and all flavored cigars.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:55.883
In this proposal,

00:12:55.883 --> 00:12:57.570
the FDA argued that these actions had

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:00.277
the potential to reduce
disease and death by quote

00:13:00.277 --> 00:13:02.280
"reducing youth experimentation

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.020
and addiction and increasing the number

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.520
of smokers that quit."

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.430
Public comments will continue
through July of 2022,

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.820
but Kinder Surprise
Eggs are already banned,

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:15.000
so the hard work has
already been accomplished.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.340
But that takes us to the
next American illegality,

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:20.430
something you potentially
might do every single day.

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:23.220
Now, if you were an
American pedestrian in 1903,

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.740
crossing the street was
a very simple endeavor.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:26.880
If you wanted to cross the street,

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.160
you would just walk across the street.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.870
Before the introduction of cars,

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.520
roads were seen as a public space

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.170
that all citizens had a right to occupy,

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:35.790
even children at play.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.800
But today, if you try and cross the street

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.660
without using a crosswalk
or cross the street

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:42.060
when the traffic light is
flashing do not walk, well,

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:46.560
congratulations, you have
committed the crime of jaywalking.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.610
Now, across the pond,

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:50.100
some of our European allies
have taken a more laissez-faire

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.580
attitude towards jaywalking
by making it totally legal.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.770
They just call it walking.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:56.640
Now, for example,

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.860
there are no laws against
jaywalking in Norway.

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.000
The same goes for the UK,

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.460
meaning that The Beatles didn't
need to use the crosswalk

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.590
for their famous "Abbey Road" cover.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.440
And the Netherlands used to
have laws against jaywalking,

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.170
but repealed these statutes in 1995

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.330
to simplify the traffic
code and give pedestrians

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.530
more freedom.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:14.363
In these countries,

00:14:14.363 --> 00:14:16.950
your right to cross the street freely

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:20.220
shall not be infringed, but
here in the United States,

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:23.370
we've taken a more punitive
approach to walking.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:24.390
Now, every year,

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.190
cities like Los Angeles issue tickets

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.890
to tens of thousands of
pedestrians for jaywalking,

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:32.070
which includes fines worth up to $200.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:33.750
But this was not always the case.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.610
In fact, ticketing someone for jaywalking

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:38.490
is a relatively young
concept in the United States.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.220
According to University of
Virginia historian Peter Norton,

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:42.480
the notion of jaywalking,

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.790
with jay being an early 20th century slur

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.920
for someone stupid or unsophisticated,

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.180
was introduced by a group of

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.580
auto industry aligned
groups in 1920s as part

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.510
of a concerted pro-car
anti-pedestrian propaganda campaign.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:55.950
But when cars were first introduced,

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.420
there were a few crosswalks
painted on the street.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.400
Pedestrians generally
ignored the ones that existed

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:00.930
'cause they didn't need to,

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.970
but as cars became more widely available,

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.520
pedestrian deaths skyrocketed
with hundreds of thousands

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.720
of Americans, many children,

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.160
being killed in car crashes

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:10.290
for the first few decades
of the 20th century.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.390
So to counter all this negative publicity,

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:14.130
auto industries sought to enact

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.420
traffic laws that would shift blame

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:20.370
from drivers and their cars
to the pedestrians themselves.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:21.690
And it worked.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.890
Not only did cities and states

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.720
begin criminalizing jaywalking,

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.040
but the US government supported the

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:29.370
anti-pedestrian propaganda
campaign by ridiculing jaywalkers

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:32.460
and placing blame on them
for automobile crashes.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.350
And today, some criminal justice advocates

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:37.530
believe jaywalking should be
decriminalized altogether.

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:38.370
But as an aside,

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.247
you should all go watch

00:15:39.247 --> 00:15:41.160
"Not Just Bikes" and get orange build

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.590
because it's kind of stupid
that we've seated all

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:47.070
of this real estate to cars
for both driving and parking

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.890
when cities should be for
the people themselves.

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:52.500
But I'll get down off of my soapbox.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.150
And while it might sound counterintuitive,

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:55.740
countries that allow jaywalking

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.360
tend to have lower traffic deaths

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.370
as pedestrians tend to cross more safely

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.920
and when they aren't worried
about criminal penalties.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.540
And criminal justice advocates point out

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.450
that jaywalking laws have
a very disparate impact

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.130
with tickets not evenly applied

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.420
and enforcement disproportionately

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.800
targeting people of color.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.180
So far, in 2021,

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.100
Virginia has heated this
call by becoming the first

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:16.650
and so far only state to
decriminalize jaywalking

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:19.470
and a similar bill to
decriminalize jaywalking was vetoed

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:22.620
by California's governor
Gavin Newsom in 2021.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.640
So, for better or worse,

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.020
if you wanna stay on
the straight and narrow

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.630
in 49 of the US states,

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.010
you'd better be sure to look both ways

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.230
and stay in the crosswalk every time.

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:32.160
For now.

